      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    X = np.load(\"vectors_secondary.npy\", mmap_mode=\"r\")\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float64)  # promote to double for accurate distances\n    n = X.shape[0]\n\n    sq_norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X)\n\n    block_size = 500\n    total = 0.0\n\n    for start in range(0, n, block_size):\n        end = min(start + block_size, n)\n        block = X[start:end]  # (b, d)\n\n        # dot products between block and all rows\n        dots = block @ X.T  # (b, n)\n\n        # squared distances: ||a||^2 + ||b||^2 - 2*a.b\n        sq_dists = sq_norms[start:end, None] + sq_norms[None, :] - 2.0 * dots\n\n        # numerical noise can create tiny negative values\n        np.maximum(sq_dists, 0.0, out=sq_dists)\n\n        dists = np.sqrt(sq_dists)\n\n        total += dists.sum()\n\n    # total is sum over all ordered pairs (including zero diagonal)\n    # Print as decimal value\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.10f}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
